<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Code</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~45 min</span>
    </div>

    <table>
        <tr><th>API</th><th>What it gives you</th><th>What it costs</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>public static StatManager Instance;</code></td>
            <td>A field that belongs to the <strong>class</strong>, not to an object — reachable
                with no reference and no search.</td>
            <td>It starts as <code>null</code>, and nothing claims it for you.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>private void Awake()</code></td>
            <td>Unity's earliest hook: it runs once per object, and every <code>Awake()</code> in a
                scene finishes before the first <code>Start()</code> runs.</td>
            <td>Order between two objects' <code>Awake()</code> methods is still not promised.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject)</code></td>
            <td>The object moves into a scene of its own that never unloads, so it survives every
                load from then on.</td>
            <td>It takes a whole <strong>GameObject</strong>, not a component.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>Destroy(gameObject)</code></td>
            <td>Removes an object — how the newcomer copy takes itself out of the game.</td>
            <td>The removal is deferred to the end of the frame: a line running later in that same
                frame can still reach it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>SceneManager.LoadScene(int buildIndex)</code></td>
            <td>What <code>SceneSwitch.cs</code> calls at every cave mouth — the line destroying your
